# Citation metadata. GitHub renders a "Cite this repository" button from this
# file and generates APA/BibTeX on demand.
#
# This exists because @furlpay/x402-guard carries an adversarial evaluation of
# the five flaw classes in Ling et al. (arXiv:2605.30998), and work that gets
# cited needs a canonical citation its author controls. Without this file a
# reviewer invents one, and the invented one is usually wrong.
#
# `preferred-citation` should be replaced with the conference entry once the
# paper is accepted — until then it deliberately points at the software, which
# is the artifact that actually exists.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FurlPay: stablecoin payment infrastructure with hardened x402 agentic payments"
message: "If you use this software or its adversarial evaluation, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ashutosh
    family-names: Kumar Singh
    email: founder@furlpay.com
    affiliation: FurlPay
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ashutosh0x/furlpay"
url: "https://furlpay.com"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - stablecoin
  - payments
  - x402
  - agentic-payments
  - account-abstraction
  - erc-4337
  - eip-7702
  - sanctions-screening
  - aml
abstract: >-
  FurlPay is a stablecoin payment platform whose x402 layer implements
  facilitator-level defences against the five flaw classes catalogued in
  "Free-Riding the Agentic Web: A Systematic Security Analysis of x402
  Payments" (Ling et al., arXiv:2605.30998): cross-resource substitution,
  duplicate-settlement race, allowance overdraft, denial of settlement and
  hidden-compute pricing. The accompanying package, @furlpay/x402-guard, ships
  an adversarial harness that reproduces each attack against an unguarded
  facilitator and measures the residual leakage with the defences enabled,
  reporting hidden-compute pricing as a mitigation rather than a fix and
  quantifying the escrow cost of closing it.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Free-Riding the Agentic Web: A Systematic Security Analysis of x402 Payments"
    authors:
      - family-names: Ling
        given-names: "" # full author list to be completed from the published paper
    year: 2026
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: "arXiv:2605.30998"
    notes: >-
      The threat model x402-guard implements defences against. Cited here
      because the harness measures itself against that paper's flaw classes.
